The forward lens maps an optional field (from.count, line 7 of 1.0) that the
data lacks, so its result is incomplete.

The evaluator positions this at the mapping itself, the most useful position of
any case here. But Translate wraps it with fmt.Errorf and cerrors.Details, so
the position survives only as text and the error carries none.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: from.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- data.json --
{"title": "a"}
-- out/error --
lens produced a non-concrete result: Translate.out.steps.0.result.count: cannot reference optional field: count:
    ship/1.0.thema:7:9
-- out/positions --
lens produced a non-concrete result: Translate.out.steps.0.result.count: cannot reference optional field: count:
	no positions
